From 15f75ac7bbc4650fae3d253b7561b0dbf9b06a82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omp <omp@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:08:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/23] ntdll/actctx: honour <probing privatePath="..."> from
 the application configuration file

Windows resolves native (non-.NET) side-by-side assemblies through the
<configuration><windows><assemblyBinding><probing privatePath="..."/> element of
<exe>.config, a documented feature since Windows 7 / Server 2008 R2 ("Application
configuration files", sbscs).  Wine's native SxS loader never read that file, so any
application shipping its dependencies in a private subdirectory listed by privatePath
failed to start with STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND (c0000135).

The Autodesk 2027 installers are such applications.  The ODIS bootstrap Setup.exe
(PE32+ x86-64, Autodesk Setup 2.24.0.9) declares the dependent assemblies odis.bs.win
and odis.bs.wx in its embedded manifest, ships them in ODIS\odis.bs.win and
ODIS\odis.bs.wx, and points at them with

  <configuration><windows>
    <assemblyBinding xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1">
      <probing privatePath="ODIS"/>
    </assemblyBinding>
  </windows></configuration>

Loaded by Wine, the three imports (wxmsw332u_core_vc_x64_custom.dll, wxbase332u_vc_x64_custom.dll,
AdHttpLib.dll) were not found and the installer could not start at all:

  fixme:actctx:parse_depend_manifests Could not find dependent assembly L"odis.bs.win" (1.0.0.0)
  err:module:import_dll Library wxmsw332u_core_vc_x64_custom.dll ... not found
  err:module:loader_init Importing dlls for ... Setup.exe failed, status c0000135

This change reads <exe>.config (the extension is replaced for a <x>.manifest source, so
exe.manifest -> exe.config, and appended otherwise, so exe.exe -> exe.exe.config), parses
the <probing privatePath> value and probes <appdir>\<privatePath>[\<assembly-name>\] -
and the same relative to the root manifest's directory - for the missing assembly, in the
same order the existing lookup uses.

Verified on this fork (wine-11.18 + patches 0001..0015):
  * raw Autodesk_Revit/AutoCAD ODIS Setup.exe from pristine media now starts
    (WINEDEBUG=+actctx shows "probing private path L\"ODIS\"", bootstrap UI appears,
    0 loader errors, no c0000135);
  * "wine kernel32_test.exe actctx": 3298 tests, 0 failures, with the new
    test_private_path covering a config-file-driven private assembly including the
    LoadLibrary redirection.

The change is upstream Wine merge request !10753 ("ntdll/actctx: Add privatePath probing
functions in SxS loader", Bolan Chen), still open/unmerged; its test suite also passes on
real Windows (Wine CI win10-21h2 jobs: kernel32:actctx 3505 assertions, 0 failures), which
is the ground truth for the element naming and probing order reproduced here.
